WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.900
The Llama family.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.425
Meta's open-weight family is the base for most industry fine-tuning,

3
00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:08.600
and its design became the standard.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:12.000
LLaMA is Meta's open-weight family.

5
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.920
It was long the default base for industry fine-tuning.

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:20.411
By twenty twenty-five Qwen overtook it in Hugging Face derivatives,

7
00:00:20.411 --> 00:00:24.433
but Llama's recipe is still the one every open model copies.

8
00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:31.533
Its design is GPT-2's skeleton, with a few upgrades that nearly every open model now copies.

9
00:00:32.733 --> 00:00:33.833
Here is the block.

10
00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.027
Tokens come in as embeddings.

11
00:00:36.027 --> 00:00:38.900
Positions are added later, inside attention.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.813
Each sublayer is preceded by RMSNorm.

13
00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:48.100
Attention uses RoPE, and later versions share key and value heads to shrink the KV cache.

14
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.433
The feed-forward network uses SwiGLU, and there are no bias terms.

15
00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:56.633
Side by side, the four upgrades are easy to see.

16
00:00:56.933 --> 00:00:59.233
RMSNorm replaces LayerNorm.

17
00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:01.367
RoPE replaces learned positions.

18
00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.300
SwiGLU replaces GELU.

19
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.300
And the bias terms disappear.

20
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.667
You can read all this from a config file.

21
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:11.667
We download the config for Llama 3.2.

22
00:01:11.967 --> 00:01:13.642
Then print four fields.

23
00:01:13.642 --> 00:01:16.774
The activation is silu, the gate in SwiGLU.

24
00:01:16.774 --> 00:01:21.800
There is an RMSNorm epsilon, a RoPE theta, and eight key value heads.

25
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.300
Here is why this vocabulary matters.

26
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:31.200
Mission notes cannot leave your network, so the assistant is a LoRA fine-tune of a Llama base.

27
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.400
It is served on your own GPU.

28
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:39.500
Quantization, KV cache growth and context stretching are all read straight from the config.

29
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.464
Let's recap.

30
00:01:41.464 --> 00:01:47.067
LLaMA's open weights were long the default base for fine-tunes, and its recipe still is.

31
00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:49.433
It uses RMSNorm and RoPE.

32
00:01:49.733 --> 00:01:51.400
SwiGLU and no biases.

33
00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:55.397
And the config file shows any model's anatomy in seconds.

34
00:01:55.397 --> 00:01:56.500
Next up: Mistral.
